{
  "answer_text": "The evidence indicates that retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) reduces the hallucination rate in several domains, but the effect is not universal and can be negligible or absent in others. Specifically, RAG significantly reduces hallucinations on science, history, law, and pop culture benchmarks, but does not measurably reduce them on trivia questions. The magnitude of reduction varies by domain, ranging from a 11.7 percentage point drop in law to a 5.2 percentage point drop in pop culture, while one study found no measurable reduction in trivia answering.",
